WEBVTT

00:00.500 --> 00:04.819
Skip counting means counting by the same jump each time.

00:05.269 --> 00:10.842
Let's count by twos. Two, four, six, eight, ten. Each hop is two.

00:11.292 --> 00:17.073
Now count by fives. Five, ten, fifteen, twenty. Each hop is five.

00:17.523 --> 00:23.096
And count by tens. Ten, twenty, thirty, forty. Each hop is ten.

00:23.546 --> 00:30.377
To find what comes next in a pattern, look at two neighbours and see how much the number grows.

00:30.377 --> 00:34.692
Ten to twenty is a jump of ten, so the next number is forty.
